course: dictionary
lesson: 3924
title: Frosty: cold weather and cold manners
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Frosty has three meanings, and the words around it tell you which one is meant. «You see your breath on a frosty morning» is about the weather: it is very cold, and there is frost (thin white ice) on the ground.
explain: Frosty can also mean covered with frost. «The same thing happens in the cracks of rocks on a frosty mountain, night after night» means the mountain is covered in frost and is very cold.
explain: Frosty can describe a person too. A «frosty look» or a frosty welcome is cold in manner, so it means unfriendly. To check, swap your meaning into the sentence: does "an unfriendly look" still make sense? If it does, you have it right.
fact: Frosty means very cold, with frost (thin white ice) on the ground and on things.
fact: Frosty can also mean covered with frost, as in «frosty grass».
fact: Frosty can describe a person who is unfriendly and cold in manner, as in «a frosty look».
fact: Frost forms when the temperature drops below 0 °C (32 °F) and water vapour freezes into ice crystals.
fact: Frosty roads and paths are slippery, so walk carefully.
exercise: «You see your breath on a frosty morning.» What does frosty mean here? | Unfriendly and cold in manner | Hot and sunny | * Very cold, with frost on the ground | Covered with snow and wet
exercise: «Her frosty look made everyone go quiet.» What does frosty mean? | * Unfriendly and cold in manner | Very loud | Warm and friendly | Covered with frost
exercise: Why are frosty paths dangerous? | Because they are hot and steep | * Because they are slippery, so you must walk carefully | Because they are too wet to see | Because they are full of sand
test: «The same thing happens in the cracks of rocks on a frosty mountain.» In this sentence, frosty means: | Wet and soft | Warm and sunny | Unfriendly | * Covered with frost
test: Which sentence uses frosty to mean unfriendly? | * A frosty welcome from the new teacher | The frosty morning was clear and bright | Frosty grass shone in the sun | The frosty path was covered in ice
exam: Frosty can mean very cold weather, covered with frost, or unfriendly in manner. In «Ben, soaked to the knees on a frosty walk, was shivering hard», which meaning fits best? | Warm and sunny | Unfriendly and cold in manner | * Very cold, with frost on the ground | Covered with wet mud
